// =============================================================================
// BreakGlass_SignIn_Alert.kql
// Author: Justin Gallimore
// Description: Monitors sign-in activity for the break glass account and alerts
//              any time it is used. Break glass accounts are emergency admin
//              accounts that exist outside of normal Conditional Access policies
//              and MFA requirements. They should almost never be used — any
//              sign-in from this account is a high-priority event that needs
//              immediate investigation.
//              This query is designed to run in Microsoft Sentinel or the
//              Log Analytics workspace connected to your Entra ID tenant.
// =============================================================================

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CONFIGURATION
// Replace the placeholder UPN with your actual break glass account UPN.
// If you have two break glass accounts (recommended) add both to the list.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
let BreakGlassAccounts = dynamic([
    "breakglass@yourdomain.onmicrosoft.com"     // Primary break glass account UPN
    // "breakglass2@yourdomain.onmicrosoft.com"  // Uncomment if you have a secondary break glass account
]);

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// MAIN QUERY
// Pull all sign-in events from the SigninLogs table for the break glass account.
// SigninLogs is populated by Microsoft Entra ID and feeds into Log Analytics
// when diagnostic settings are configured to export sign-in logs.
// We look back 90 days by default — adjust the TimeGenerated filter as needed.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated >= ago(90d)                          // Look back 90 days — adjust as needed
| where UserPrincipalName in (BreakGlassAccounts)          // Filter to break glass accounts only
| project                                                   // Select only the fields we care about
    TimeGenerated,                                          // When the sign-in occurred
    UserPrincipalName,                                      // Which break glass account was used
    AppDisplayName,                                         // What application was accessed
    IPAddress,                                              // Where the sign-in came from
    Location,                                               // Geographic location of the sign-in
    ResultType,                                             // 0 = success, anything else = failure code
    ResultDescription,                                      // Human-readable result description
    ConditionalAccessStatus,                                // Whether CA policies applied
    AuthenticationRequirement,                              // MFA required or single factor
    DeviceDetail,                                           // Device information if available
    RiskLevelDuringSignIn,                                  // Entra ID risk score at time of sign-in
    RiskLevelAggregated,                                    // Aggregated risk level for the identity
    CorrelationId                                           // Use this to correlate with other log tables
| extend SignInResult = iff(ResultType == 0, "SUCCESS", strcat("FAILED - Code: ", tostring(ResultType)))
| extend AlertSeverity = iff(ResultType == 0, "HIGH", "MEDIUM")  // Successful break glass sign-ins are HIGH severity
| sort by TimeGenerated desc                                // Most recent sign-ins first

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// NOTES FOR PRODUCTION USE
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. In Microsoft Sentinel, wrap this query in a Scheduled Analytics Rule
//    with a frequency of 5 minutes and a lookback of 1 hour to get near
//    real-time alerting on any break glass usage.
//
// 2. Set the alert severity to High and route it to your SOC or on-call team
//    immediately. Break glass usage should never go uninvestigated.
//
// 3. The ConditionalAccessStatus field confirms whether CA policies applied.
//    For a properly configured break glass account this should show "notApplied"
//    since the account is excluded from all CA policies by design.
//
// 4. Correlate any hits against AuditLogs to see what actions were taken
//    during the break glass session:
//
//    AuditLogs
//    | where CorrelationId == "<CorrelationId from SigninLogs result>"
//    | project TimeGenerated, OperationName, Result, InitiatedBy, TargetResources
// =============================================================================
